A few options:
(a) resize and compress on the client before uploading, which cuts payload size about 5x for phone photos;
(b) switch to direct-to-S3 presigned uploads so files skip our API servers entirely;
(c) move thumbnail generation off the request path into the background queue.
They're independent. (b) is the biggest win but it also means changes in the iOS and Android apps, not just the web client.
